@startuml
title Merchant requests a journey explanation after a failed action
autonumber

actor "AI shopping agent" as Agent
participant Merchant
participant "MerchantJourneyController" as API
participant "JourneyQueryService" as Query
participant "JourneyReadRepository" as Repo
database PostgreSQL as DB

Agent -> Merchant : Receives failed cart or payment result
Merchant -> API : GET /api/v1/journeys/{journeyId}?merchantId={merchantId}
API -> Query : getJourney(merchant, journeyId)
Query -> Repo : Find journey matching journeyId and merchantId
Repo -> DB : Read journey ownership
DB --> Repo : Matching journey or no row
Repo --> Query : Journey summary or not found
alt Journey belongs to merchant
Query -> Repo : Read journey status, operations, events, decisions
Repo -> DB : Select journey and correlated evidence
DB --> Repo : Journey rows and ordered history
Repo --> Query : Structured journey facts
Query -> Query : Assemble response from recorded facts
Query --> API : JourneyDetail
API --> Merchant : Timeline, outcome, Guard reasons, next-step context
Merchant --> Agent : Explain the confirmed reason to the shopper
else Journey missing or owned by another merchant
Query --> API : Not found
API --> Merchant : 404
end

note over Query,DB
Return recorded facts and Guard reasons.
Do not invent or change the Guard decision.
The merchantId query value is a demo ownership check,
not authentication. Replace it with authenticated identity
before exposing the endpoint beyond the local demo.
end note
@enduml
